-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 2, §2.10 גננת בגן משולב
-- The integrated kindergarten: when a regular kindergarten is one, who
-- staffs it, and keeping the management allowance.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `2.10 גננת בגן משולב`

DECLARE `kindergarten class` HAS
    `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` IS A NUMBER
    `of them sensory-impaired`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `pupils in all`                                                          IS A NUMBER

§§ `2.10.6 Conditions of service`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_1 A heading ("definition").

-- 1 ¶2: a regular kindergarten is integrated if 8-10 children referred to the
-- placement committee, which recommended placing them there, are integrated
-- in it, with at least 22 pupils in all; if the integrated pupils are
-- sensory-impaired, 6-8 of them and at least 18 in all. F-2.10-a: a group
-- of whom only some are sensory-impaired is not addressed; the sensory rule
-- is read as applying only when all of them are.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_1/p2
GIVEN k IS A `kindergarten class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `integrated under the general rule` k IF
        k's `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` AT LEAST 8
    AND k's `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` AT MOST 10
    AND k's `pupils in all` AT LEAST 22

GIVEN k IS A `kindergarten class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `integrated under the sensory rule` k IF
        k's `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` AT LEAST 6
    AND k's `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` AT MOST 8
    AND k's `pupils in all` AT LEAST 18

GIVEN k IS A `kindergarten class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an integrated kindergarten` k IF
    IF k's `of them sensory-impaired` EQUALS k's `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation`
       AND k's `of them sensory-impaired` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `integrated under the sensory rule` k
    ELSE `integrated under the general rule` k

`five sensory-impaired and two other integrated children among 20` MEANS
    `kindergarten class` WITH
        `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` IS 7
        `of them sensory-impaired`                                               IS 5
        `pupils in all`                                                          IS 20

`a partly sensory-impaired group falls between the two rules` MEANS
        `integrated under the sensory rule` `five sensory-impaired and two other integrated children among 20`
    AND NOT `integrated under the general rule` `five sensory-impaired and two other integrated children among 20`
#ASSERT `a partly sensory-impaired group falls between the two rules`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_2 A heading ("staffing and conditions of service").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_2/p2
DECLARE `integrated-kindergarten staff` IS ONE OF
    `integrating head kindergarten teacher`
    `integrated kindergarten teacher`
    `pedagogical assistant to the teacher`
    `kindergarten assistant`

`the staff of an integrated kindergarten` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_2/p3
        `integrating head kindergarten teacher`,
        @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_2/p4
        `integrated kindergarten teacher`,
        @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_2/p5
        `pedagogical assistant to the teacher`,
        @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6__para_2/p6
        `kindergarten assistant`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6/p1 Introduces the summary table of the staff's conditions of service, a linked document whose content is not in this text.

-- ¶2: an integrated kindergarten teacher in integrated kindergartens who
-- received the management allowance for 8 years keeps it; one who served
-- less goes to an exceptions committee (the conditions-of-service department,
-- chair; the Treasury; the Teachers' Union).
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6/p2
DECLARE `management-allowance outcome` IS ONE OF
    `keeps the management allowance`
    `goes to the exceptions committee`

GIVEN `years with the management allowance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `management-allowance outcome`
DECIDE `keeping the management allowance` `years with the management allowance` IS
    IF `years with the management allowance` AT LEAST 8
    THEN `keeps the management allowance`
    ELSE `goes to the exceptions committee`

`the exceptions committee` MEANS
    LIST `the conditions-of-service department`, `the Treasury`, `the teachers' union`

`the exceptions committee's chair` MEANS `the conditions-of-service department`

-- "תחולה: מכ"ב באלול התשנ"א (1.9.91)".
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6/p3
`2.10.6 applies from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1991

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6/p4 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6/p5 A source: director-general's circular נח/9(ב), section 16.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_10__ssec_2_10_6/p6 A source: director-general's circular נב/1, section 27; wage agreement of 18.12.01 (l4/agreements/teachers-general/2001-12-18_histadrut-hamorim_wage-agreement-1999-2001.l4).

-- Worked examples.
`nine integrated among 24` MEANS
    `kindergarten class` WITH
        `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` IS 9
        `of them sensory-impaired`                                               IS 0
        `pupils in all`                                                          IS 24
#ASSERT `an integrated kindergarten` `nine integrated among 24`
#ASSERT NOT `an integrated kindergarten` `five sensory-impaired and two other integrated children among 20`
#ASSERT `keeping the management allowance` 5 EQUALS `goes to the exceptions committee`

§§ `Property checks`

-- The section's rules over their whole finite space: 0 to 12 integrated
-- children, every number of them sensory-impaired, 14 to 26 pupils in all,
-- and 0 to 12 years with the management allowance.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `kindergarten class`
DECIDE `a checked class` n s p IS
    `kindergarten class` WITH
        `integrated children placed on the placement committee's recommendation` IS n
        `of them sensory-impaired`                                               IS s
        `pupils in all`                                                          IS p

`the pupil counts checked` MEANS range 14 26

-- 2.10.6.1: a class with no integrated child is never integrated, and one
-- more pupil never takes the status away.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN s YIELD
                        all (GIVEN p YIELD
                                    (n GREATER THAN 0 OR (NOT `an integrated kindergarten` (`a checked class` n s p)))
                                AND ((NOT `an integrated kindergarten` (`a checked class` n s p))
                                     OR `an integrated kindergarten` (`a checked class` n s (p PLUS 1))))
                            `the pupil counts checked`)
                    (range 0 n))
            (range 0 12)

-- The two rules agree with the clause where it speaks: a group with no
-- sensory-impaired child is integrated exactly at 8-10 among 22 or more,
-- and a wholly sensory-impaired group exactly at 6-8 among 18 or more.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                            `an integrated kindergarten` (`a checked class` n 0 p)
                            EQUALS (n AT LEAST 8 AND n AT MOST 10 AND p AT LEAST 22)
                        AND (    n EQUALS 0
                              OR `an integrated kindergarten` (`a checked class` n n p)
                                 EQUALS (n AT LEAST 6 AND n AT MOST 8 AND p AT LEAST 18)))
                    `the pupil counts checked`)
            (range 0 12)

-- F-2.10-a over every partly sensory-impaired group: the two rules part on
-- 6-7 integrated children among 18 or more, on 8 among 18-21, and on 9-10
-- among 22 or more — so the case the clause does not address is decisive
-- across that whole range, not at one count.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the two rules part on` n p IF
    NOT (    `integrated under the sensory rule` (`a checked class` n 1 p)
         EQUALS `integrated under the general rule` (`a checked class` n 1 p))

#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                        `the two rules part on` n p
                        EQUALS (    (n AT LEAST 6 AND n AT MOST 7 AND p AT LEAST 18)
                                 OR (n EQUALS 8 AND p AT LEAST 18 AND p AT MOST 21)
                                 OR (n AT LEAST 9 AND n AT MOST 10 AND p AT LEAST 22)))
                    `the pupil counts checked`)
            (range 2 12)

-- 2.10.6 ¶2 over 0 to 12 years: she keeps the allowance exactly from eight
-- years, and more years never send her back to the committee; the
-- committee's chair is one of its members.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN y YIELD
                    (`keeping the management allowance` y EQUALS `keeps the management allowance`) EQUALS (y AT LEAST 8)
                AND (    `keeping the management allowance` y EQUALS `goes to the exceptions committee`
                      OR `keeping the management allowance` (y PLUS 1) EQUALS `keeps the management allowance`))
            (range 0 12)
#ASSERT elem `the exceptions committee's chair` `the exceptions committee`
